## HEAVY (the machine is shared; the machine is the limit)
At most TWO heavy jobs run machine-wide across all MPS lanes. A heavy job = `dotnet build`, `dotnet test` (the whole solution or a whole project), a mutant batch, `bash scripts/package.sh`. A single-class `dotnet test --filter` run after a build is light only if it adds no build; a mutant run that rebuilds is heavy. Take a slot by atomic `mkdir '/Volumes/Datasec_DEV/!CODING/Datasec/Datasec MPS Commercial Calculator/.tools/.heavy-lock-1'` (else `-2`; neither free: poll every 60 s), write `holder.txt` (pane name, label, `date`) inside, run ONE job, release by MOVING the holder file to `.tools/b1511/logs/` and `rmdir` your own dir. **Load gate: `LC_ALL=C uptime` load1 under 24 on TWO reads 120 s apart (the reads are not independent: say so)** (the product owner's 2026-11-11 ruling that the limit scales to this 18-CPU machine, RELAYED from the L2 kit's Stamp S4 and the L1 kit's HEAVY; Stamp S4 here confirms or changes it). A holder directory older than 30 minutes with no live pane is REPORTED, never removed. A wait is not a finding; waited 60 minutes: say so; at the hard stop: `BLOCKED: heavy lock waiting at load <n>`. Timing is not asserted anywhere in this lane. Light work (reading, the Edit tool, git reads, `gh` GETs, Jira GETs) needs no lock. UNMEASURED by the drafter: how long the full dotnet suite takes on this machine at the present load (the L2 kit's STATUS may hold a figure; read it).

